{"availability":"available","full":"ClarkEL-99/drawsy-ai","name":"drawsy-ai","description":"AI-powered visual workspace for drawing, planning, building, and working with connected context.","category":"Design","language":null,"stars":0,"forks":5,"created":"2026-07-24T06:05:23Z","updated":"2026-07-18T17:36:19Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://drawsy.adarsh.rocks","topics":[],"demo":"https://drawsy.adarsh.rocks/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T09:26:53.575Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T09:26:53.575Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T09:26:53.575Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T09:26:53.575Z","stars":0,"forks":5}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A visual workspace where ideas, project context, connected tools, and a coding agent meet on an infinite canvas.","Drawsy turns the whiteboard into an active workspace. The same hand-drawn canvas can hold diagrams, presentations, project plans, source material, generated images, and a live application preview. Its side-by-side AI surface can understand the current workspace, use explicitly attached context, and propose or apply editable canvas changes."],"features":["the Excalidraw editor and its open, editable scene model;","Drawsy workspaces for canvases, presentations, Kanban, Jira, and connected sources;","a model-flexible agent surface: Codex or OpenCode, with the same workspace contract, visible tool progress, and Markdown responses;","deterministic visual documentation through DRAW.md;","real-time collaboration and remote asset storage; and"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ClarkEL-99/drawsy-ai/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"065c8c18f3933efb0d05fded11999848f56df35e6a1eb4db505436f2c6f8b7f2","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T09:26:53.901Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T09:26:53.901Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A visual workspace where ideas, project context, connected tools, and a coding agent meet on an in